{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: recover the remaining head-notice and cold-read availability outcome of retired #144, after the current #19971, #19986 and #19996 queue. Deliver the remaining justified work to main. The retirement explicitly retained the substance and required remeasurement; this request supplies a current baseline and preserves the parts already delivered.\n\nCurrent evidence at 6f4864fdaf2069f9ab917286e537db05bea12f51: [service.wait](internal/service/server.go@6f4864fdaf2069f9ab917286e537db05bea12f51:398) still creates a 250 ms polling clock per call and invokes Snapshot on every check. [snapshotFlight](internal/app/app.go@6f4864fdaf2069f9ab917286e537db05bea12f51:2457) already shares cancellation-independent verified rebuild work; [snapshotWithSource](internal/app/app.go@6f4864fdaf2069f9ab917286e537db05bea12f51:2490) keeps its cache/read/audit/fold under the snapshot mutex. [Current architecture](docs/reference/architecture.md@6f4864fdaf2069f9ab917286e537db05bea12f51:264) permits bounded polling to notice Git changes made by other processes. This does not require one Git polling loop per waiter.\n\nThe attached [baseline evidence](head-wait-evidence.json), [probe](head-wait-probe.go) and [output](head-wait-output.txt) come from a disposable current-head test repository. At depths 1 and 31, three 1.1-second runs each: one waiter made five Git ref reads, eight aligned waiters also made five, and eight staggered waiters made 39–40. The old claim that every waiter always multiplies reads is too broad: current single-flight coalesces overlap. These are small-depth warm baselines, not external-change latency measurements or full acceptance evidence.\n\nComplete the remaining outcome:\n\n1. Give resident waiters a shared per-log head-change notification mechanism with bounded cost independent of idle waiter count, preserving notice of ordinary Git updates from other processes. Reuse the existing flight and live runtime; keep kernel and generic live layers free of Workroom policy. Preserve composite cursor behavior, actor-specific inbox isolation, live-only wakes, reset/generation handling, timeout and cancellation, missed-wakeup protection, and honest verification/refusal when a head moves, rewinds or becomes invalid. No second cache, second verifier or fake current answer.\n2. Assess and resolve the remaining previous-snapshot availability condition against the current contract. Where a previously verified, still interpretable snapshot is safe to expose during a rebuild, make it available with an explicit old-frontier/rebuilding qualification; it must not authorize an act or claim currentness. A prior projection invalidated by a profile change must remain unavailable. If current contracts admit no safe previous-snapshot scenario, establish that with specific paths and evidence and obtain a durable scope disposition before treating this condition as satisfied; do not silently omit it. Any new governed interpretation or trust-policy choice must be proposed for ordinary adoption before implementation.\n3. Measure before and after at stated scaled depths and waiter counts, with aligned and staggered starts. Separate Git process count, warm timeout cost, external durable-change wake latency, live-only wake latency, and cold-rebuild/read availability. Preserve existing cancellation-independent single-flight and atomic publication tests, and add omission-sensitive controls for the actual notification mechanism and its failure paths. Performance measurements belong in the existing evidence lane, not scheduler-sensitive correctness assertions. Do not claim depth-20k or physical-resource properties from the attached small fixture.\n\nBegin on request/shared-head-notices from then-current main. Reconcile the cited behavior bases; ordinary inherited staleness alone does not require refiling. Publish exact-path artifacts and applicable architecture/guidance changes on current behavior provenance. Obtain fresh independent Architecture, Security and Simplification review of the exact final head; ratify approval, seal the main merge, push origin/main, check resulting CI and remove the owned worktree and branch. A diagnosis or notifier-only patch does not by itself close all conditions. No real telemetry restart, installation, repository reset, forge setting, key operation or log migration is authorized by this request.","body":{"conditions":"Complete the remaining shared per-log head notification and safe prior-snapshot availability outcome of #144, with current scaled before/after measurements; preserve delivered single-flight and verified atomic publication. Independent exact-head review, sealed main merge, push/CI/cleanup.","head":"6f4864fdaf2069f9ab917286e537db05bea12f51","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:092bd6cbe60056cd85ba626ea22807c1e97cc376, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:9032b1529724a17ee2a200a01363a61ab8d76325 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:07e8e48166ea90a1d864c829f36902817926f6e7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:15f25225ffe951e89eda7c2de4cb5f51c5ab71a0, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:17daa8a1f7100fef505641e20f0b7a2d212c8fef and 67 more","target_head":"6f4864fdaf2069f9ab917286e537db05bea12f51","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}